# Copy to .env and fill in real values locally. Never commit .env — see
# docs/project-knowledge/06-CODING-STANDARDS.md "Environment & Secrets".
# In deployed environments (Fly.io), set these as secrets, not plain env vars.

# PostgreSQL connection string. Shape below matches Neon's pooled connection
# string (what this project actually uses — see
# docs/runbooks/database-migrations.md) rather than a generic local Postgres
# URL: a "-pooler" host, and both `sslmode=require` and `channel_binding=require`
# in the query string (Neon rejects a plain unencrypted connection). Get the
# real value from the Neon console's "Connection string" panel, or from Fly
# secrets for the deployed environment — never from chat, a commit, or a PR.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<password>@<project>-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech/<database>?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require

# Anthropic API key for the AIService boundary (see 05-ARCHITECTURE.md §5).
# Real keys look like `sk-ant-api03-<~100 more characters>` — get one from
# console.anthropic.com. Not yet actually called anywhere in apps/api; this
# is a placeholder ahead of EPIC 4/8 (AI quiz engine, doubt assistant).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-replace-with-a-real-key

# Port the NestJS server listens on. Falls back to 8080 if unset (see main.ts).
PORT=8080

# Origin allowed to make cross-origin requests (the web app). Falls back to
# the Next.js dev default (http://localhost:3000) if unset (see main.ts). In
# production this is the real Vercel Production URL for apps/web — exact
# scheme+host, no path, no trailing slash (see docs/runbooks/deploy-api.md
# "CORS Configuration" for the full explanation and a live curl check), e.g.:
#   ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://taps-web-eta.vercel.app
ALLOWED_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# Signs/verifies the admin JWT (see docs/adr/005-admin-auth-and-validation.md
# and docs/api/auth.md). Any long random string; e.g. generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string

# bcrypt hash of the single admin password (never the plaintext — see the
# same ADR). Generate with:
#   node -e "require('bcryptjs').hash(process.argv[1], 10).then(console.log)" 'your-chosen-password'
ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=$2b$10$replace.with.a.real.bcrypt.hash.................
